# eOn SVN r2549. HarnessCounter through ext_pot. Kernel lj_cut.
# L-BFGS memory 20 on the 1000 LJ38 starts at force sigma 0. Settings match eon-svn/lbfgs-m20 except the potential: unshifted lj/cut, epsilon 1, sigma 1, cutoff 40, which is the problem potential, not lj_cluster. converged_force in this file is the clean tolerance 0.01. The run sets the client tolerance to max(0.01, 3 * sigma * sqrt(114)). When sigma is positive, a force sample under that threshold is held above it until the clean energy over the last 5 evaluations spans at most max(1e-10, 3 * sigma). The seed for start i is 20261016 + i. Success also requires a clean vibrational Hessian index of 0, with the six rigid modes removed. Energy and Kabsch RMSD are not applied: the problem file has no per-start reference. r2549 does not read energy_weighted, ci_mmf, climbing_image_band_slack, setup_mmf_peaks, or the develop L-BFGS catalog past memory, inverse curvature, max inverse curvature, auto scale, and the two resets. Those keys are omitted. The keys it does read sit in [Optimizer]. The binary is SVN r2549, the registry pin. Export of the 2014 revision is forbidden, so this row is r2549.
# Final energy is the clean lj/cut value of min.con. Coordinates are the endpoint sidecar. A dissociated cluster is divergence.
counter harness
code Eon svn
code_version r2549
commit r2549
algorithm LBFGS
tuning default
template eon-svn/lj38-noise-0
problem minimization/lj38-noise
reducer harness
cap 10000
n 1000
par2_mean 300.052
nfailed 5
mean_calls 200.9
median_calls 189.0
min_calls 100.0
max_calls 575.0
n_crash 0
n_divergence 0
n_cap 0
n_wrong_stationary 5
energy_min -173.2523779009367
energy_max -145.6711278988844
